# Headers for the static assets, applied by Cloudflare Workers at the edge.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL: /data/space.json is published for other Seattle
# Makers web projects to read, and a browser on another origin cannot read it
# without an access-control-allow-origin header. Astro is `output: 'static'`,
# so that endpoint is prerendered to a file and served by the Worker's ASSETS
# binding - a header set on the Response inside space.json.ts is built away and
# never reaches anybody. It has to be set here.
#
# It is the same wall /today runs into from the other side: seattlemakers.org
# sends no such header, which is the entire reason worker/index.js exists.
#
# ONLY `npm run serve` CAN VERIFY THIS. Neither `astro dev` nor `astro preview`
# goes through the Worker, so both will happily serve the file with no header
# and no complaint.

/data/*
  access-control-allow-origin: *
  cache-control: public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=86400
